      "table_comment": "Conversion funnel in long format for the dashboard funnel chart. Grain: one row per CHANNEL x STAGE_ORDER, 5 channels x 5 stages (1 Impressions, 2 Clicks, 3 Leads, 4 Converted leads, 5 Purchases) = 25 rows, full range 2023-01-01..2025-12-31, no date dimension. Built from MART_CHANNEL_PERFORMANCE, so each stage adds up to the known total over the 5 channels (impressions 436,844,819; clicks 7,102,319; leads 261,684; converted leads 39,696; purchases 16,691). Chart it with STAGE as the dimension (or a STAGE filter): STAGE_VALUE is additive across channels, never across stages (different units). PREV_STAGE_VALUE and TOP_OF_FUNNEL_VALUE are additive across channels too, so stage conversion = SUM(STAGE_VALUE) / SUM(PREV_STAGE_VALUE) and share of top of funnel = SUM(STAGE_VALUE) / SUM(TOP_OF_FUNNEL_VALUE) are correct at any channel filter. No ratio is stored and there is no 'ALL' channel row (it would double count every SUM). An aggregate campaign funnel, not a per-person journey: converted leads = trials + purchases (a lead converts at most once), and Purchases is the subset of converted leads that converted to a purchase, not a later step for the same person. Synthetic data. Built by dbt (models/marts/mart_conversion_funnel.sql, added in Phase 6; no hand-written SQL twin).",
